---
import Guide from '../../layouts/Guide.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const withBase = (p = '') => (base.endsWith('/') ? base : base + '/') + p;
---

<Guide
  title="Read the Bhagavad Gita in Nepali (नेपाली)"
  description="Read the full Bhagavad Gita in Nepali (भगवद्गीता नेपालीमा) — every verse in the original Sanskrit with a Nepali translation and context, free online. Switch between Nepali, Hindi and English any time."
  slug="bhagavad-gita-in-nepali"
  datePublished="2026-10-04"
>
  <p>
    The Bhagavad Gita is read all over Nepal and by Nepali speakers everywhere, but a clear,
    gentle Nepali reading of the whole text — verse by verse, with the original Sanskrit beside it —
    is surprisingly hard to find online. Gita Daily offers exactly that: every one of the 701 verses
    with a Nepali translation (नेपाली अनुवाद) and a short context, free to read.
  </p>

  <h2>What you get in Nepali</h2>
  <p>
    On every verse you can switch the translation to <strong>Nepali (नेपाली)</strong> and read the
    meaning in plain, natural Nepali — not a word-for-word transliteration of Hindi, but genuine
    Nepali with its own grammar and voice. Alongside it you'll find the original Sanskrit, and you can
    switch to Hindi (हिन्दी) or English whenever you like. Each verse also carries a short note of
    context, so you're never reading a line out of nowhere.
  </p>

  <h2>A note on the translation</h2>
  <p>
    The Nepali translations are carefully prepared and are being refined with native-speaker review,
    so if a line can read more naturally, it will keep improving over time. The aim is simple: that a
    Nepali reader feels the verse was written for them, in their own language.
  </p>

  <h2>Where to begin</h2>
  <p>
    A gentle first chapter to read in Nepali is <a href={withBase('gita/2')}>Chapter 2</a> — often
    called the heart of the Gita. From there, <a href={withBase('gita/12')}>Chapter 12</a> on
    devotion is short and warm. Or open the <a href={withBase('gita')}>full chapter index</a> and
    pick wherever you feel drawn. A good single verse to sit with is
    <a href={withBase('gita/2/47')}>Bhagavad Gita 2.47</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>On your phone, in Nepali</h2>
  <p>
    The free Gita Daily app keeps the Nepali reading in your pocket, adds a verse each day, and lets
    you start from a mood to find a verse for the moment — all with the Nepali, Hindi and English
    translations together. The whole scripture stays free, always.
  </p>
</Guide>
